WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.330
After months of colorful
teasers and posters,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.940
Warner Bros. has finally dropped

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.750
the first official trailer
for "Birds of Prey."

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.590
From its references to the
Joker to this adorable hyena,

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.123
here's everything you
missed in the new trailer.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.160
The trailer begins with Harley Quinn

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.404
announcing her breakup with the Joker.

00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:26.860
Harley: The Joker and I broke up.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.100
Narrator: This changes
everything for Harley,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.227
including a new haircut and
a symbolic change in attire.

00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:35.940
"Suicide Squad" showed
Harley wearing a T-shirt

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.710
with a reference to the Joker,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.130
while the new Harley
Quinn symbolically wears

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.200
an outfit with her name on it,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.010
identifying her as a more
independent character.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.950
The song that plays throughout the trailer

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.300
is Édith Piaf's "L'Hymne à l'Amour,"

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.300
or "The Hymn to Love."

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.970
It's an obviously ironic choice for a song

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.580
that exemplifies the
love-and-hate relationship

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.800
between Joker and Harley.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.320
So, how does Harley try to move on?

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.430
By burning down a building, of course.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.960
A shot from the trailer
shows Harley burning down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.950
the Ace Chemicals factory,

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.840
a location that essentially created

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.600
both Joker and Harley Quinn

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.390
and was also featured
briefly in "Suicide Squad."

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.790
The same factory seems
to later be inspected by

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.940
none other than Renee Montoya,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.690
a detective from Gotham City

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.800
who never technically was a
member of the Birds of Prey

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.430
but has had a history of
accompanying them in comics.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.360
And, speaking of Montoya, we see some of

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.465
the other official
members of Birds of Prey.

00:01:34.465 --> 00:01:37.970
Like Black Canary, portrayed
by Jurnee Smollett-Bell,

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.670
working as a singer at a nightclub.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.070
And this cool shot briefly
hints at her superpower,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.603
the "canary cry," her ability to let out

00:01:46.603 --> 00:01:48.570
an ultrasonic scream.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.210
The cup is shaking from her singing.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.850
Perhaps she doesn't yet understand
the extent of her power.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.270
We also get a better look at the Huntress,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.690
a lethal vigilante played
by Mary Elizabeth Winstead.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.140
The character also made an
appearance in CW's "Arrow."

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.500
And from the looks of it,
it seems like the Huntress

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.510
is already very much active,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.620
serving justice with
her trademark crossbow.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.920
And finally, Cassandra Cain,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.370
an assassin who once took
the mantle of Batgirl

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.970
in the comics.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.250
While she was always portrayed

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.220
as having difficulty with
speech, this adaptation

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.350
seems to have no trouble
bantering with Harley.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.170
So it's safe to assume that the filmmakers

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.810
are taking the most
liberty with the character,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:33.490
the film being one of her
first live-action adaptations.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.610
And, for the first time,

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.200
we get a look at them together as a team.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.200
The Birds of Prey.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.960
So, what brings these
unlikely characters together?

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.240
The best guess is this man, Roman Sionis,

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.600
or Black Mask,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.460
an infamous villain from
the "Batman" comics.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.950
While he's a villain most well
known for his iconic mask,

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.700
we never see it in the trailer,

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.170
although it's heavily
foreshadowed throughout,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.690
such as from these dancers in the club

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.280
or the painting behind him

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.580
during what happens to be
his psychotic breakdown.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.290
But for now, Ewan McGregor
seems to be playing Roman Sionis

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.580
before he becomes Black Mask,

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.260
also suggested by these
initials on his gloves.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.350
The trailer also implies that Roman has

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.200
an obsession with Harley.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.365
We also see Harley performing
in Roman's nightclub,

00:03:28.365 --> 00:03:30.228
a scene that is a direct homage

00:03:30.228 --> 00:03:33.272
to Marilyn Monroe's performance in 1953's

00:03:33.272 --> 00:03:35.220
"Gentlemen Prefer Blondes."

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.730
It's also the same nightclub

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.073
that Black Canary performs
in and meets Harley.

00:03:40.073 --> 00:03:43.090
Perhaps the two characters bond
with their hatred for Roman

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.980
and recruit the help of others
to fight a common enemy.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.340
And perhaps the fight
turns Roman to Black Mask.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.980
And is that when he
hires the help of Zsasz,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.670
another famous "Batman" villain

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.010
we get a glimpse of in the trailer?

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.740
We can only predict for now.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.090
And, of course, it's impossible
not to talk about the hyena.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.520
The trailer shows Harley adopting a hyena

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.850
from an exotic pet shop

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.160
and even reenacting a scene
from the "Lady and the Tramp."

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.957
This is a concept that first appeared in

00:04:11.957 --> 00:04:14.320
"The Batman Adventures: Mad Love."

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.610
But the hyenas are more popularly known

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.250
for their appearances in
"Batman: The Animated Series."

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.140
What's odd is that there's
supposed to be two of them,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:26.650
Bud and Lou, named after
the two famous comedians

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.310
Abbott and Costello.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.720
So, where is the other one?

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.810
The hyenas aren't the only reference to

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.460
the animated series.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.710
An outfit that Harley wears in this shot

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.450
closely resembles her attire

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.850
in the episode "Harley's Holiday,"

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:44.350
which also features Harley
firing a cork as a weapon,

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.440
similar to how she fires a beanbag

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.110
to knock out an officer in the film.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.393
Fun note: You can see various items

00:04:51.393 --> 00:04:53.257
throughout the letters of the title

00:04:53.257 --> 00:04:55.440
that symbolize the different characters,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.590
like this arrow that
symbolizes the Huntress;

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.340
Harley's hammer, which can be found here;

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.435
and a razor and brass knuckle

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:06.300
that most likely belong to Zsasz.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.860
So, was there anything we missed?

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.523
Let us know in the comments.

